  "body": "The spec says \"When a user agent is to handle a resource obtained from a fetch as a download, it should provide the user with a way to save the resource for later use, if a resource is successfully obtained; or otherwise should report any problems downloading the file to the user.\".\r\n\r\n\"Report any problems\" is a little vague, maybe an error event should be fired on the <a> element? And if fetching returns an error, e.g. 404, should UAs still try to download?",
